 "serial": "7",
 "title": "CHAPTER VII ## PREMISES OF DACOITY AND ROBBERY The cases registered under the heads 'Dacoity' and 'Robbery' in the country were further analysed according to the place of occurrence of these two crimes. The highest number of Dacoity cases (7391) was committed in residential premises and only one case of Bank Dacoity was reported out of a total of 10910 cases during 1976. Similar was the position under 'Robbery', where too the highest number of cases (6016) was committed. In residential premises, followed by Robbery on highways (3158) and only four cases of 'Robbery' in Banks were reported out of a total of 17974 cases during 1976. The relevant statistics may be seen in Tables 50 and 51.",
 "listing_title": "Premises of Dacoity and Robbery Burglary & Theft",
